    "recommendations": "• Mark the driveway entrance with reflective address numbers visible from both directions on the road.\n• Post address numbers on any detached structures to help responders identify buildings during multi-unit operations.\n• Keep a diagram of the property near the front entry showing the location of all structures, the storage area, and the equipment storage area.\n• Clear the access drive of parked vehicles and stored equipment to maintain an unobstructed path to all structures.\n• Keep all perimeter fence gates unlocked or secured with a break-away lock to allow responders to reach the rear of the property without delay.\n• Mark the rear access point with a reflective marker so responders can locate it quickly from outside the fence line.\n• Identify a flat, firm staging area on the open lawn large enough for emergency vehicles to position away from structures.\n• Keep the walkways between structures clear of stored materials, equipment, and debris to allow responders to move between buildings on foot.\n• Label the storage area and equipment storage area with visible signage so responders can identify contents without entering blindly.\n• Confirm that the access drive can support the weight of a fire apparatus by verifying surface condition and width are adequate for a large vehicle to reach all structures."
